==============================================================================
H047 -- DOES THE NOETHER-CHARGE FREE DUST CLUSTER AT SMALL SCALES?
==============================================================================
  H0 = 67.4 km/s/Mpc, h = 0.674, Om = 0.315, OL = 0.685, n_s = 0.9649
  rho_Lambda = 5.8450e-27 kg/m^3 ; c/H0 = 4448.0 Mpc
  a_0 (postulate, both footings run) = 9.3619e-11 and 1.1279e-10 m/s^2
  a_0 recomputed from 0.5 c sqrt(G rho_L) = 9.3624e-11 m/s^2  (consistency, not a result)

==============================================================================
PART 1 -- (a) DOES A CONSERVED CHARGE FREE-STREAM?
==============================================================================

  WDM (thermal relic, g = 1.5, T = T_nu):
      T_nu,0 = 1.9454 K = 1.6764e-04 eV ;  <q> = 5.2830e-04 eV
      m =  1.0 keV : v_0 =     158.4 m/s   lambda_fs =   2.0519 Mpc ( 1.3830 h^-1 Mpc)   k_fs =    4.54 h/Mpc
      m =  2.0 keV : v_0 =      79.2 m/s   lambda_fs =   1.1109 Mpc ( 0.7487 h^-1 Mpc)   k_fs =    8.39 h/Mpc
      m =  3.5 keV : v_0 =      45.3 m/s   lambda_fs =   0.6739 Mpc ( 0.4542 h^-1 Mpc)   k_fs =   13.83 h/Mpc
      m =  5.3 keV : v_0 =      29.9 m/s   lambda_fs =   0.4641 Mpc ( 0.3128 h^-1 Mpc)   k_fs =   20.09 h/Mpc

  THE NOETHER CHARGE:
      f(x,v) = n(x) delta^3(v - v(x))   -- a DELTA FUNCTION in velocity
      second central moment  <(v - <v>)^2>  =  0 identically
  [PASS] N1 [NO VELOCITY DISPERSION] a coherent field has exactly one velocity at
      each event, so its dispersion -- the second central moment, the only
      thing free-streaming consumes -- vanishes identically
         measured : sigma^2: WDM(3.5 keV) = 2.0477e+03 m^2/s^2 ; Noether charge = 0.0000e+00 m^2/s^2
         threshold: sigma^2(charge) < 1e-6 * sigma^2(WDM)
         This is the structural point. Free-streaming is NOT 'motion' -- every
                  component of the universe moves. It is the SPREAD of velocities
                  about the mean. A delta function has none.
  [PASS] N2 [NO FREE-STREAMING LENGTH] lambda_fs = int (sigma/a) dt = 0 for the
      charge, while WDM of every viable mass has a finite one
         measured : lambda_fs: WDM(3.5 keV) = 0.6739 Mpc ; Noether charge = 0.0000 Mpc
         threshold: lambda_fs(charge) < 1e-3 * lambda_fs(WDM 3.5 keV)
         The WDM cutoff is set by lambda_fs. With lambda_fs = 0 there is no cutoff.
                  This is a consequence of the degree of freedom being a COHERENT FIELD,
                  not of the value of a_0 -- so it survives H029's circularity audit.

  WHY THE VLASOV PICTURE IS THE WRONG ONE:
      grad_mu[f'(K) d^mu phi] = 0  <=>  [f' g^{mu nu}
           + (2 f''/Lam^4) d^mu phi d^nu phi] grad_mu grad_nu phi = 0
      -> quasilinear SECOND-order hyperbolic: characteristics at speed c_s.
      -> Vlasov would be FIRST order: df/dt = 0 along dx/dt = v.
  [PASS] N3 [HYPERBOLIC, NOT VLASOV] the perturbation equation's characteristic
      speed is c_s, not a particle velocity; with c_s = 0 the cone
      collapses and there is no propagation at all
         measured : characteristic speed = c_s = 0.0000e+00 m/s ; WDM particle speed = 4.5251e+01 m/s
         threshold: c_s < 1e-3 * c  (i.e. no propagating cone)
         A pressureless medium does not disperse a wave; it simply falls. The
                  only k-dependence in the growth equation is the Poisson term, which
                  is k-independent in real space -- see Part 5.

==============================================================================
PART 2 -- (b) IS THERE A TURNOVER SCALE FROM a0 AND Lambda?
==============================================================================

  THE JEANS LENGTH with c_s = 0:
      lambda_J = c_s sqrt(pi/(G rho))   ->  0 identically
  [PASS] N4 [NO JEANS SCALE] with c_s = 0 the Jeans length is identically zero,
      so pressure cannot stabilise any mode on any scale
         measured : lambda_J = 0.0000e+00 Mpc  (c_s = 0, rho = rho_m(z=0))
         threshold: lambda_J < 1e-6 * (c/H0)
         Leg (ii) of the WDM argument is gone as well. Both legs need a nonzero
                  microphysical speed, and both are zero here.

  EVERY SCALE THAT a0 AND Lambda CAN MAKE:
      quantity                                 footing 1       footing 2   verdict
      footing 1: c^2/a0 =   31111.92 Mpc   c/sqrt(G rho_L) =   15555.17 Mpc   (c/H0 = 4448.0 Mpc)
      footing 2: c^2/a0 =   25823.81 Mpc   c/sqrt(G rho_L) =   15555.17 Mpc   (c/H0 = 4448.0 Mpc)

      (c^2/a_0)/(c/H_0) = c H_0/a_0 = [6.9947, 5.8058]
      -> H029 PROVED c H_0/a_0 is algebraically IDENTICAL to the postulate.
         Both of these are the postulate restated. EXCLUDED, not claimed.
      (c/sqrt(G rho_L))/(c/H_0) = sqrt(8 pi/(3 Om_L)) = 3.4971  -> same circular family. EXCLUDED.

  THE ONE NON-CIRCULAR SCALE -- and it needs a mass:
        M [Msun] r_M = sqrt(GM/a0) [kpc], footing 1      footing 2
           1e+10                              3.859          3.515
           1e+11                             12.202         11.117
           1e+12                             38.586         35.154
           1e+13                            122.020        111.167
           1e+14                            385.860        351.541
           1e+15                           1220.197       1111.672
  [PASS] N5 [NO P(k) TURNOVER] the only non-circular scale a0 makes is
      r_M = sqrt(G M / a_0), which requires a mass: it is a per-object
      HALO scale, not a k-space turnover
         measured : r_M spans 3.859 -> 1220.197 kpc as M spans 1e10 -> 1e15 Msun (2.50 decades in r for 5 in M)
         threshold: r_M must depend on M (span > 1 decade) => no k-independent turnover exists
         CONCLUSION FOR (b): there is NO turnover scale. lambda_J = 0, c^2/a_0 and
