==============================================================================
PART 3 -- THE SOUND SPEED OF THE ACTUAL f (mu_2 branch)
==============================================================================

  DERIVATION (exact, no approximation):
      c_s^2 = (dp/dK)/(drho/dK) = f' / (f' + 2 K f'')
      with u = sqrt(K), f' = mu_2(u), 2K f'' = u mu_2'(u), and
      mu_2'(u) = 2/(1+u)^3   (differentiate mu_2 = u(2+u)/(1+u)^2)
      => c_s^2 = mu_2/(mu_2 + u mu_2') = (u^2+3u+2)/(u^2+3u+4) = 1 - 2/(u^2+3u+4)

       u=sqrt(K)       mu_2       f(K)      c_s^2      c_s/c
          0.0000    0.00000   -1.00000   0.500000   0.707107
          0.0500    0.09297   -0.99984   0.518362   0.719974
          0.2000    0.30556   -0.99131   0.568966   0.754298
          0.5000    0.55556   -0.89426   0.652174   0.807573
          1.0000    0.75000   -0.38629   0.750000   0.866025
          1.2235    0.79773   -0.00070   0.781837   0.884215
          2.0000    0.88889    2.13611   0.857143   0.925820
          5.0000    0.97222   22.08315   0.954545   0.977008
         20.0000    0.99773  394.81572   0.995690   0.997843
  [PASS] N6 [THE SOUND SPEED IS HEALTHY] c_s^2 of the frozen scalar stays inside
      (0,1) on the whole physical branch -- the pre-registered falsifier
      'c_s^2 leaving [0,1] anywhere -> dead' is NOT triggered
         measured : c_s^2 over u in (0, 20]: min = 0.500000 (at u->0+), max = 0.995690 (at u=20)
         threshold: 0 < c_s^2 < 1 everywhere on u > 0
         Sub-luminal (causal) and positive (no gradient instability, given f'>0).
                  The completion is healthy. But note what it is NOT: it is not zero.

  THE w = 0 (dust background) POINT: p = Lam^4 f(K) = 0 at u* = 1.223856
      rho/Lam^4 = 2 u*^2 mu_2(u*) = 2.389921   -> w = 0 exactly
      BUT c_s^2(u*) = 0.781883   -> c_s = 0.884242 c
  [PASS] N7 [c_s^2 = 0 IS A SECTOR INPUT, NOT A STATE OF f] the frozen scalar
      never has c_s^2 = 0: it is >= 1/2 for u >= 0 and strictly positive on
      the whole domain u > -1. The 'sound speed exactly zero' free dust must
      come from a sector with rho proportional to the charge, not from f.
         measured : min c_s^2 on u >= 0 is c_s^2(0) = 0.500000; at the w=0 dust point c_s^2(u*=1.2239) = 0.781883
         threshold: for c_s^2 = 0 to be a state of f we would need min c_s^2 < 1e-3; measured 0.5 > 1e-3 => the statement 'it is an input' holds
         STATED PLAINLY: the prediction in Part 5 is CONDITIONAL. The framework
                  posits the free dust as a separately-conserved charge sector with
                  rho proportional to n and c_s^2 = 0. This lane verifies that c_s^2 = 0
                  is NOT supplied by the frozen-scalar f -- it is a sector property,
                  and it is an OPEN structural requirement, not a derived result.

  CONSEQUENCE -- THE k-ESSENCE FLUID ITSELF CANNOT CLUSTER:
      k_J = a sqrt(4 pi G rho_tot)/c_s ;  k_horizon = a H/c
      in matter domination  k_J/k_horizon = sqrt(1.5 Om(a))/c_s
      at the dust point (Om(a)->1): k_J/k_horizon = 1.385080
  [PASS] N8 [THE SCALAR FLUID IS JEANS-STABLE ON EVERY SUB-HORIZON SCALE]
      with c_s ~ 0.88 c the Jeans wavenumber exceeds the horizon
      wavenumber, so no sub-horizon mode of the k-essence fluid can grow
         measured : k_J/k_horizon = 1.385080 at u* = 1.2239 (c_s = 0.8842 c)
         threshold: k_J/k_horizon > 1  (all sub-horizon modes stabilised)
         This is why the free dust CANNOT be the k-essence fluid. If it were, the
                  framework would predict NO dark-matter clustering at all, and would be
                  dead. The two-state architecture (H032) needs the dust sector.

==============================================================================
PART 4 -- (c) THE SMALL-SCALE MATTER POWER SPECTRUM
==============================================================================

  WITH c_s = 0 THE GROWTH EQUATION HAS NO k:
      ddotdelta + 2 H deltadot + (c_s^2 k^2/a^2) delta = 4 pi G rho delta
      c_s = 0  =>  the k-term is absent  =>  delta(k,a) = delta(k,a_i) D(a)/D(a_i)
      =>  P(k,a)/P(k,a_i) = [D(a)/D(a_i)]^2   INDEPENDENT OF k

  THE SHAPE IS THEREFORE INVARIANT, AND IT IS THE LCDM SHAPE:
       k [h/Mpc]       T_BBKS    n_eff = dlnP/dlnk    n_s-4+2/ln(2.34q)
           0.100  1.84781e-01              -1.2242              17.5255
           1.000  7.09866e-03              -2.2837              -2.2017
          10.000  1.35197e-04              -2.6135              -2.6098
         100.000  2.01118e-06              -2.7498              -2.7496
  [PASS] N9 [GROWTH IS SCALE-FREE] P(k,a)/P(k,a_i) = D(a)^2 is the same number at
      k = 0.1 and k = 100 h/Mpc: the transfer function is k-independent
         measured : ratio at k=0.1: 25.000000000000 ; at k=100: 25.000000000000 ; |difference| = 0.000e+00
         threshold: |difference| < 1e-9
         Zero k-dependence is exactly what CDM does and exactly what WDM does not.
                  No damping term, no free-streaming integral, nothing k-dependent
                  enters the growth equation.

  THE PREDICTION, AND THE CONTRAST:
       k [h/Mpc]    R = P_fw/P_LCDM    WDM 1.0 keV    WDM 3.5 keV    WDM 5.3 keV
           0.100           1.000000       0.999943       0.999997       0.999999
           1.000           1.000000       0.990132       0.999560       0.999843
          10.000           1.000000       0.206676       0.926623       0.973132
          50.000           1.000000       0.000000       0.086532       0.386379
         100.000           1.000000       0.000000       0.000290       0.022320

      (WDM column: Bode-Ostriker-Turok / Viel et al. fitting form
       T = (1 + (alpha k)^{2 nu})^{-5/nu}, nu = 1.12,
       alpha = 0.049 (m/keV)^-1.11 (Om/0.25)^0.11 (h/0.7)^1.22 h^-1 Mpc;
       R = T^2.  Cross-checked against the first-principles lambda_fs of
       Part 1: k_fs(1 keV) = 4.54 h/Mpc vs a fitted
       half-mode of 6.77 h/Mpc -- agree to a factor ~2, the expected
       definitional spread.)
  [PASS] N10 [THE KEPLER-GRADE DISCRIMINATOR] the framework predicts R(k) = 1 at
      EVERY k -- no cutoff, no break -- while a 3.5 keV thermal relic
      predicts R(100 h/Mpc) of order 1e-4
         measured : R_framework(100 h/Mpc) = 1.000000 ; R_WDM(3.5 keV, 100 h/Mpc) = 2.904601e-04 ; R_WDM(3.5 keV, 10 h/Mpc) = 0.926623
         threshold: |R_framework - 1| < 1e-12  AND  R_WDM(3.5 keV, 100) < 1e-2
         FOUR ORDERS OF MAGNITUDE between the two predictions at k = 100 h/Mpc.
                  That is a measurement, not an interpretation: a Lyman-alpha or
                  high-z-galaxy P(k) that shows a cutoff kills the framework, and one
                  that shows none kills WDM.
  [PASS] N11 [THE SLOPE] the framework's small-scale slope is exactly the LCDM
      slope -- n_eff -> n_s - 4 = -3.035 with the log running +2/ln(2.34 q)
         measured : n_eff: k=1 -> -2.2837 ; k=10 -> -2.6135 ; k=100 -> -2.7498 ; asymptote n_s-4 = -3.0351
         threshold: |n_eff(k=100) - (n_s - 4 + 2/ln(2.34 q))| < 0.05
         THE SPECIFIC PREDICTION: P(k) ~ k^{n_s} T_CDM^2(k) with NO cutoff, i.e.
                  n_eff(1 h/Mpc) = -2.28, n_eff(10 h/Mpc) = -2.61, and
                  n_eff -> n_s - 4 = -3.0351 asymptotically. Every one of these
                  numbers is the LCDM number: the framework's free dust is
                  INDISTINGUISHABLE FROM CDM in the linear power spectrum.

==============================================================================
PART 5 -- THE CIRCULARITY AUDIT (H029)
==============================================================================

  H029 PROVED that c H_0/a_0, the seesaw and Z are algebraically IDENTICAL to
  the postulate a_0 = (1/2) c sqrt(G rho_Lambda). They are unifications, not
  confirmations, and must not be re-presented as new.

  WHERE a_0 ENTERS THIS LANE:
    * Part 1 (does a conserved charge free-stream?):  NO a_0, NO Lambda.
      Follows from the coherent-field nature of J^mu and c_s = 0.
    * Part 2 (is there a turnover?):  a_0 enters -- and the ONLY scale it can
      make, c^2/a_0, is EXACTLY the circular quantity
      (c^2/a_0)/(c/H_0) = c H_0/a_0.  EXCLUDED, not claimed.
    * Part 4 (the power spectrum):  NO a_0, NO Lambda.  R(k) = 1 follows from
      the absence of a k-dependent term in the growth equation.

  WHERE Lambda ENTERS: only through the sound speed of f (Part 3), where it
  cancels -- c_s^2 is dimensionless and f-independent of Lambda^4.

  [PASS] N12 [NOT CIRCULAR] the prediction R(k) = 1 and its slope do not use the
      value of a_0 or of Lambda, and the one place a_0 could enter
      (the turnover scale) is precisely the H029-circular quantity
         measured : a_0 appears only in: ['part2 (excluded as circular)']; c H_0/a_0 = [6.9947, 5.8058] = the postulate itself
         threshold: a_0 and Lambda enter the R(k)=1 derivation 0 times, and the only a_0 scale is flagged circular
         Per H029's own list of genuinely non-circular results ('cluster shape: the
                  phantom slope -- independent of a_0's value'), this belongs in that
                  class: it survives even if the postulate's coefficient is wrong.

==============================================================================
H047 READING:  12 PASS / 0 FAIL
==============================================================================

THE PREDICTION
--------------
    R(k) = P_framework(k) / P_LCDM(k) = 1      for EVERY k, no cutoff.
    n_eff(k) = n_eff^LCDM(k):  -2.28 at 1 h/Mpc, -2.61 at 10 h/Mpc,
                               -2.75 at 100 h/Mpc -> n_s - 4 = -3.035 asymptotically.

    vs 3.5 keV thermal-relic WDM:  R(10 h/Mpc) = 0.93, R(100 h/Mpc) = 2.9e-04.
    Four orders of magnitude of separation at k = 100 h/Mpc.

WHY: (a) a coherent conserved charge has ZERO velocity dispersion (delta
function in v), so lambda_fs = 0 -- free-streaming has nothing to eat; and the
dynamics is a second-order hyperbolic PDE at speed c_s, not Vlasov transport.
(b) With c_s = 0 the Jeans length is identically zero, and the only scale a_0
and Lambda can build, c^2/a_0, is the postulate restated. (c) The growth
equation therefore loses its only k-dependent term, so the shape of P is
invariant and equals the CDM shape.

IS IT CIRCULAR?  No. Neither a_0 nor Lambda enters parts (a) or (c). The single
place a_0 could enter -- the turnover scale -- is exactly c H_0/a_0, which H029
proved is algebraically the postulate; it is excluded here, not claimed.

THE HONEST CAVEAT
-----------------
    c_s^2 = 0 is NOT a state of the frozen-scalar f. We derived, exactly,
        c_s^2(u) = (u^2+3u+2)/(u^2+3u+4) = 1 - 2/(u^2+3u+4),
    which is >= 1/2 for u >= 0 and strictly positive on all u > -1; at the
    w = 0 dust point u* = 1.2235 it is c_s^2 = 0.782 (c_s = 0.884 c). Hence
    the k-essence fluid is Jeans-stable on every sub-horizon scale
    (k_J = 1.386 k_horizon) and CANNOT be the dark matter. The free dust must
    be a distinct, separately-conserved charge sector with rho proportional to
    n and c_s^2 = 0. The prediction above is conditional on that sector, and
    supplying it is an OPEN structural requirement -- flagged, not assumed away.

WHAT THIS LANE DOES NOT DO
--------------------------
    It does not distinguish the framework from LCDM. R(k) = 1 says the free
    dust is INDISTINGUISHABLE from CDM in the linear power spectrum. The
    framework's discriminating small-scale signature is the PHANTOM sector
    (H036: outer density slope -2 vs NFW -3), not the free dust. The value of
    this prediction is that it kills WDM, and it is falsified BY any detected
    small-scale cutoff, not by agreement with LCDM.

{"pass": 12, "fail": 0}
